1
00:00:00,140 --> 00:00:01,847
You already planned the week.

2
00:00:01,847 --> 00:00:05,085
Morning comes and you open the
whole list again, as if last

3
00:00:05,085 --> 00:00:08,539
night never happened. Write one
next-action default before you sleep.

4
00:00:08,539 --> 00:00:11,916
After this video you will have one
written next-action default sitting where

5
00:00:11,916 --> 00:00:15,294
tomorrow-you will see it first, so the
morning starts execution instead of

6
00:00:15,294 --> 00:00:18,191
reopening every open loop. You will
pick the sentence tonight, put it

7
00:00:18,191 --> 00:00:22,728
on one surface, and refuse to
browse the rest of the list

8
00:00:22,728 --> 00:00:24,279
until that sentence is done or rewritten.

9
00:00:24,279 --> 00:00:26,269
Here is the stall in plain steps.

10
00:00:26,269 --> 00:00:29,583
You sit down. You open
the planner or the board.

11
00:00:29,583 --> 00:00:31,672
You reread titles you already chose.

12
00:00:31,672 --> 00:00:35,769
You compare them. Nothing feels
ready, so you check messages to warm

13
00:00:35,769 --> 00:00:39,566
up. Twenty minutes later you
have a new ranking and no started

14
00:00:39,566 --> 00:00:41,397
work. The list is not the problem.

15
00:00:41,397 --> 00:00:43,325
Reopening the list is the problem.

16
00:00:43,325 --> 00:00:45,494
A weekly plan is a menu.

17
00:00:45,494 --> 00:00:49,411
A morning that treats the
menu as a decision again is a

18
00:00:49,411 --> 00:00:52,849
second planning session. A written
next-action default is one sentence that names

19
00:00:52,849 --> 00:00:55,002
the first verb, the
object, and where it lives.

20
00:00:55,002 --> 00:00:57,272
Not a theme. Not a priority label.

21
00:00:57,272 --> 00:01:00,403
A verb. Open the draft in this folder.

22
00:01:00,403 --> 00:01:02,973
Send the invoice sitting in this file.

23
00:01:02,973 --> 00:01:05,909
Write it before the morning, because
morning-you wants a fresh ranking.

24
00:01:05,909 --> 00:01:08,661
Night-you still remembers
which item was actually next.

25
00:01:08,661 --> 00:01:10,830
Put the sentence on one surface.

26
00:01:10,830 --> 00:01:14,067
If it lives inside a long
list, it is still a list.

27
00:01:14,067 --> 00:01:17,724
If you cannot name a verb
tonight, the plan is not a

28
00:01:17,724 --> 00:01:22,602
plan yet. Pick the smallest started
item from yesterday and write that.

29
00:01:22,602 --> 00:01:23,709
The default can be ugly.

30
00:01:23,709 --> 00:01:25,116
It cannot be a menu.

31
00:01:25,116 --> 00:01:28,149
Install it as a physical
default, not a mood.

32
00:01:28,149 --> 00:01:32,726
Choose one surface tomorrow-you will
touch before any app that contains a

33
00:01:32,726 --> 00:01:34,658
list. The card in front of the keyboard.

34
00:01:34,658 --> 00:01:37,109
The first line of a paper index card.

35
00:01:37,109 --> 00:01:39,521
A lock-screen note that
is only this sentence.

36
00:01:39,521 --> 00:01:43,255
Not a dashboard. Write the
sentence as verb, object, place.

37
00:01:43,255 --> 00:01:47,793
Open section two of the client memo
and write the missing paragraph.

38
00:01:47,793 --> 00:01:50,447
Record the first take already
sitting in the project folder.

39
00:01:50,447 --> 00:01:53,662
Reply to the one starred
email, then close the client.

40
00:01:53,662 --> 00:01:57,639
Add a stop rule on the
same card: do not open the

41
00:01:57,639 --> 00:02:01,275
weekly list until this sentence is
finished or replaced in writing.

42
00:02:01,275 --> 00:02:04,592
Without the stop rule the card
is decoration and the list wins.

43
00:02:04,592 --> 00:02:07,165
Put the weekly list out
of the first glance.

44
00:02:07,165 --> 00:02:09,454
Close the tab. Hide the board.

45
00:02:09,454 --> 00:02:13,970
Leave the planner in the drawer
until the default is done.

46
00:02:13,970 --> 00:02:15,539
You are not deleting the plan.

47
00:02:15,539 --> 00:02:17,367
You are stopping another planning meeting.

48
00:02:17,367 --> 00:02:20,882
Test it tonight. Sit down
as if it were morning.

49
00:02:20,882 --> 00:02:22,629
Look only at the card.

50
00:02:22,629 --> 00:02:25,118
Start the verb for two minutes.

51
00:02:25,118 --> 00:02:29,035
If you immediately want the full
list, the sentence is still a

52
00:02:29,035 --> 00:02:33,412
category. Rewrite it smaller. Failure
mode one: you write a theme instead

53
00:02:33,412 --> 00:02:34,881
of a verb. Finish the report.

54
00:02:34,881 --> 00:02:37,430
Work on the course. Catch up.

55
00:02:37,430 --> 00:02:41,727
Those reopen ranking. Rewrite until a
stranger could start without asking you

56
00:02:41,727 --> 00:02:43,056
what it means. Name the file.

57
00:02:43,056 --> 00:02:46,527
Name the section. Name
the first two minutes.

58
00:02:46,527 --> 00:02:49,477
Failure mode two: you keep three defaults.

59
00:02:49,477 --> 00:02:52,067
That is a list with better stationery.

60
00:02:52,067 --> 00:02:56,185
One sentence. If a second item
matters, it waits until the first

61
00:02:56,185 --> 00:02:58,618
is done or the sentence
is rewritten on purpose.

62
00:02:58,618 --> 00:03:02,855
Failure mode three: the default
lives inside the same app that holds

63
00:03:02,855 --> 00:03:06,332
the whole inventory. You open
the app to read the default and

64
00:03:06,332 --> 00:03:08,261
the inventory is already on screen.

65
00:03:08,261 --> 00:03:12,057
Move the sentence out. Paper
beats a board you must unlock.

66
00:03:12,057 --> 00:03:14,590
A dedicated note beats
a task tool with badges.

67
00:03:14,590 --> 00:03:18,806
Failure mode four: you rewrite the
default every morning before starting.

68
00:03:18,806 --> 00:03:21,259
That is the old stall with a new name.

69
00:03:21,259 --> 00:03:25,196
You may rewrite it only after
two minutes of the current verb,

70
00:03:25,196 --> 00:03:27,508
or the night before. Morning
rewriting is ranking.

71
00:03:27,508 --> 00:03:31,284
When a morning goes wrong,
do not add a new system.

72
00:03:31,284 --> 00:03:33,754
Inspect the card. Was there a sentence.

73
00:03:33,754 --> 00:03:36,747
Was it a verb. Was the list visible first.

74
00:03:36,747 --> 00:03:41,644
Fix that one surface. The mechanism
stays the same: a written next-action

75
00:03:41,644 --> 00:03:44,859
default so the morning does
not reopen the whole list.

76
00:03:44,859 --> 00:03:47,572
Run it for one workday as a closed loop.

77
00:03:47,572 --> 00:03:51,949
Tonight, pick the verb from work
that is already open, not from

78
00:03:51,949 --> 00:03:54,241
a fantasy week. Write it on the surface.

79
00:03:54,241 --> 00:03:56,548
Put the list away. Sleep.

80
00:03:56,548 --> 00:04:00,945
Tomorrow, sit down and start the
sentence before mail, chat, or the

81
00:04:00,945 --> 00:04:04,500
board. Use a two-minute
timer if you need a fence.

82
00:04:04,500 --> 00:04:07,814
When the timer ends you
may continue the same verb.

83
00:04:07,814 --> 00:04:11,210
You may not open the inventory
to hunt a better feeling.

84
00:04:11,210 --> 00:04:15,007
If the sentence was wrong, replace
it in writing after those two

85
00:04:15,007 --> 00:04:17,396
minutes, then start the new verb.

86
00:04:17,396 --> 00:04:20,570
Do not replace it in your
head while scrolling titles.

87
00:04:20,570 --> 00:04:22,342
The replacement must
land on the same surface.

88
00:04:22,342 --> 00:04:25,816
At shutdown, write tomorrow's
sentence before you close the machine.

89
00:04:25,816 --> 00:04:27,484
That is the whole system.

90
00:04:27,484 --> 00:04:30,014
No new app. No extra review meeting.

91
00:04:30,014 --> 00:04:32,505
The weekly plan can stay where it is.

92
00:04:32,505 --> 00:04:34,093
The morning reads one line.

93
00:04:34,093 --> 00:04:38,270
After three mornings, look only
at this: did you start the written

94
00:04:38,270 --> 00:04:39,719
verb before you reopened the list.

95
00:04:39,719 --> 00:04:41,886
If yes, keep the surface.

96
00:04:41,886 --> 00:04:45,020
If no, the surface is
still losing to a list.

97
00:04:45,020 --> 00:04:48,758
Move the card closer to the first
glance and make the sentence

98
00:04:48,758 --> 00:04:50,928
smaller. Do not add a second board.

99
00:04:50,928 --> 00:04:54,765
Before you stand up, write one next-action
sentence for tomorrow: verb, object,

100
00:04:54,765 --> 00:04:59,342
place. Put it on one surface
you will see before any list.

101
00:04:59,342 --> 00:05:03,360
Add the stop rule: do not open
the weekly list until that

102
00:05:03,360 --> 00:05:04,467
sentence is done or rewritten.

103
00:05:04,467 --> 00:05:07,980
That is the default.
Use it in the morning.
